@startuml
title Data-Flow Diagram — Level 1 (OKS MCP Request Processing)

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam rectangleBorderThickness 1
left to right direction

rectangle "Developer /\nCoding Agent" as User
rectangle "1. Validate input\nand classify intent" as P1
rectangle "2. Retrieve relevant\nschema and examples" as P2
rectangle "3. Translate and\nvalidate OksQuery" as P3
rectangle "4. Execute approved\nread-only query" as P4
rectangle "5. Serialize bounded\nMCP response" as P5
rectangle "LLM API" as LLM
database "D1: Schema cache /\nindex" as D1
database "D2: TDAQ/OKS\ndata files" as D2

User --> P1 : question + version
P1 --> P2 : valid request + target hints
P2 --> D1 : lookup schema metadata
D1 --> P2 : class / attribute slice
P2 --> P3 : schema slice + few-shot examples
P3 --> LLM : translation / repair prompt
LLM --> P3 : candidate OksQuery
P3 --> P4 : validated OksQuery
P4 --> D2 : query selected data file
D2 --> P4 : matching objects
P4 --> P5 : structured result set
P5 --> User : query, count, results, warnings

note bottom of D2
  The executor filters before results cross
  the MCP boundary; the full configuration is
  never returned to the agent.
end note
@enduml
